![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When loading parsed files, we must validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, skip bad entries, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed. Currently, `indexRows` silently skips malformed rows or rows missing `question_key` without recording diagnostics. We should explicitly check for and record malformed entries as structured validation failures.

```javascript
function indexRows(rows, role, diagnostics) {
  const map = new Map();
  asArray(rows).forEach((row, index) => {
    if (!row || typeof row !== 'object' || Array.isArray(row)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_row',
        role,
        row_index: index,
        reason: 'row_is_not_an_object',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
      return;
    }
    if (!row.question_key) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_row',
        role,
        row_index: index,
        reason: 'missing_question_key',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
      return;
    }
    if (map.has(row.question_key)) return;
    map.set(row.question_key, { row, index });
  });
  return map;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When loading parsed files (such as JSON), validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, skip bad entries, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed.
</details>

