When sorting alphanumeric or potentially non-numeric identifiers like `question_key`, avoid using simple byte-order comparisons or arithmetic subtraction which can yield unstable sorting or errors. Instead, use a null-safe natural string comparison to ensure robust and consistent sorting of the generated artifacts.

```javascript
function compareRows(left, right) {
  const leftKey = left?.question_key;
  const rightKey = right?.question_key;
  if (leftKey == null && rightKey == null) return 0;
  if (leftKey == null) return 1;
  if (rightKey == null) return -1;
  return String(leftKey).localeCompare(String(rightKey), undefined, { numeric: true, sensitivity: 'base' });
}
```

